# Build context exclusions for the API image.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS: backend/api/Dockerfile does `COPY backend /app/backend`, and there
# was no .dockerignore, so the image carried the WHOLE backend directory -- 11 GB, of
# which ~1.6 MB is actual API code. Measured on the kiosk 2026-08-30:
#
#     backend/data          9.9 GB   the MBTiles archives
#     backend/audio_files   766 MB   dispatch recordings
#     backend/models         73 MB   model caches
#     backend/cfr_dispatch + api + scripts   ~1.6 MB   <- what the API needs
#
# All of that bulk is BIND-MOUNTED at runtime by docker-compose.yml:
#
#     - ./backend/audio_files/recordings:/app/backend/audio_files/recordings
#     - ./backend/data:/app/backend/data
#
# so the baked-in copy is shadowed the instant the container starts and is never
# read. It was pure dead weight: a 22 GB image, ~10 minutes of "exporting layers" on
# every rebuild, and 168 GB of accumulated images on the kiosk.
#
# It was also quietly misleading -- the image held a FROZEN snapshot of the tiles and
# recordings from whenever it was last built, which would be served if a mount were
# ever missing. Absent data failing loudly beats stale data served silently.

# --- The bulk, all mounted at runtime ---
backend/data/
backend/audio_files/
backend/models/

# --- Never belongs in a runtime image ---
backend/tests/
backend/migrations/
*.log
*.log.*
dispatch.log*
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# --- Frontend: the API serves none of this ---
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/src/

# --- Repo furniture ---
.git/
.github/
docs/
.agents/
.claude/
*.md
!backend/api/requirements.txt

# --- Secrets must never enter an image layer ---
.env
*.env
!.env.example
backend/.env
backend/.env.*
frontend/.env.local
